{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1785002780,"nonce":"ioQ+m+Im+gw7rjU28dtt6ZkfvXE=","message":"Fix in PR #79 (branch `fix/dogfood-run-as-root-workspace-write`, commit 86c45a1). The literal case was already fixed on main by 2fb0b9b (post-restore `chmod -R g+rwX` + `g+s`). The remaining hole: gid-65532 membership was only a side effect of the Pod-level `fsGroup`, which a uid-pinning sidecar service takes (ADR-0058) — so a workspace step with e.g. `services: [{postgres:16, run_as_user: 999}]` silently lost the workspace group. Now every workspace Pod carries `supplementalGroups: [WORKSPACE_GID]`; ADR-0039 baseline unchanged. NOT live-verified on a cluster. Leaving open until the PR merges.","files":null}]}